config RTC_QTI_GLINK
	tristate "QTI Glink RTC"
	depends on RTC_CLASS && QTI_PMIC_GLINK
	help
	  Say Y here to enable the Qualcomm Technologies, Inc. RTC driver
	  for platforms where direct SPMI access to PMIC RTC hardware is
	  restricted.

	  On these platforms (such as Hamoa), the RTC hardware permissions
	  are managed by a remote processor that handles the TAD (Time and
	  Alarm Device) feature. This driver acts as a proxy, communicating
	  over PMIC Glink to query time and program alarms, allowing the
	  RTC to wake up or interrupt the APPS subsystem.

	  To compile the driver as a module, choose M here: the module will be
	  called rtc_qti_glink.
